1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:05,640
Being alone kind of sucks so why has it become an aesthetic.
一个人待着有点难受，那它为什么反而成了一种审美风格？

2
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:12,280
Spend a day alone with me in new York a productive day alone friday night alone it's everywhere and I made this content too.
“跟我在纽约独处一天”“高效独处的一天”“独自度过周五夜晚”，到处都是，我自己也做过这种内容。

3
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:22,030
But I keep wondering has being alone actually just become an aesthetic or is that just how we're coping with the fact that being alone just kind of sucks.
但我一直在想：独处真的只是成了一种风格，还是说我们在用这种方式应对独处确实有点难受的事实？

4
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:28,919
When you're a kid being alone doesn't mean anything I would spend hours by myself drawing random flags or learning magic tricks to show my family.
小时候，独处并不意味着什么。我会自己花上好几个小时画各种旗子，或者学魔术表演给家人看。

5
00:00:28,919 --> 00:00:33,080
And it just was nobody thought that it was sad I definitely didn't think it was sad.
事情就是这样，没人觉得很可怜，我自己当然也不觉得。

6
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:37,720
But at some point I don't know exactly when but being alone started to mean something about you.
但不知从什么时候开始，我说不准，独处开始像是在说明你是一个什么样的人。

7
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:43,240
Like if you were home alone on a friday night you felt like you were missing out on something shouldn't you have more plans more friends.
比如周五晚上一个人在家，你会觉得自己错过了什么：难道不该有更多安排、更多朋友吗？

8
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:46,190
I think my relationship with being alone has evolved a lot over the years.
我觉得这些年来，我与独处的关系已经变化了很多。

9
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:51,880
Sometimes it's great and I love it but sometimes I hate it and like I said before really sucks.
有时它很棒，我很喜欢；但有时我讨厌它，就像之前说的，真的不好受。

10
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:57,400
And now instead of asking why being alone feels so bad we're filming it nicely and calling it a vibe.
现在，我们不再问为什么独处感觉这么糟，而是把它拍得很好看，然后说这是一种氛围。

11
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:04,680
This video isn't about romanticizing being alone it's about why being alone feels so loaded now and how to deal with the lingering feeling of loneliness.
这段视频想谈的是：为什么独处如今承载了这么多情绪，以及怎么面对那种挥之不去的孤独感，而不是把独处浪漫化。

12
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:07,950
I want to pause for a second because I know this doesn't apply to everyone.
我想先停一下，因为我知道这些感受并不适用于所有人。

13
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:15,800
Some people genuinely love being alone and I think that's important to say because enjoying solitude isn't something you need to grow into or learn how to.
有些人确实喜欢独处，我觉得这一点要说清楚，因为享受独处不一定是需要慢慢成熟才懂或后天学会的事。

14
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:21,000
For some people it's just natural they recharge alone they think better alone they feel calmer when there's space around them.
对有些人来说，这很自然。他们独处时恢复精力，思考更清楚，周围留有空间就更平静。

15
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,920
So when I say being alone kind of sucks I'm not saying that as a universal truth.
所以当我说独处有点难受时，并不是在说这是一条适用于所有人的真理。

16
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:32,199
I'm talking about a specific kind of aloneeness the kind that feels imposed unwanted or maybe loaded with some sort of meaning.
我说的是某一种独处：它是被迫的、不想要的，或者被赋予了某种意味。

17
00:01:32,199 --> 00:01:37,390
The problem isn't being alone it's when being alone feels like something happened to you instead of something you chose.
问题不在独处本身，而在于你感觉独处是降临到你身上的事，而非自己的选择。

18
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:44,199
Chosen solitude feels grounding imposed aloneeness feels like rejection all that I loved I loved alone.
自愿的独处让人安定，被迫独处却像遭到了拒绝。“我所爱的一切，我都独自去爱。”

19
00:01:44,199 --> 00:01:52,440
This angsty quote by edgar alan poe couldn't be more accurate when you're 8 years old with a sketchbook this is just a fact this is just accurate it's not tragic.
这句有苦闷情绪的诗句，作者说出自坡，真是再贴切不过。八岁时拿着速写本独处，只是事实，并不悲惨。

20
00:01:52,440 --> 00:02:00,910
But now at 23 years old it sounds devastating because somewhere we started equating being alone with being lonely and being lonely with losing.
但到了二十三岁，听起来就令人难过了，因为不知何时起，我们把独处等同于孤独，又把孤独等同于失败。

21
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,559
I'm thinking back on the times in my life when I felt the most alone.
我在回想人生中感到最孤单的那些时候。

22
00:02:03,559 --> 00:02:07,719
My first semester of college after my first breakup my first year in new York after graduation.
比如大学的第一个学期、第一次分手后，以及毕业后在纽约的第一年。

23
00:02:07,719 --> 00:02:13,480
But what's interesting is I wasn't actually alone that much I had roommates I went to class I showed up to things.
但有意思的是，我其实并没有经常一个人待着。我有室友，会去上课，也会参加一些活动。

24
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:19,080
But I felt lonely in this very specific way it was this lack of belonging the sense that I didn't have my people.
可我会以一种很特别的方式感到孤独：缺少归属感，感觉没有自己的那群人。

25
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:26,359
And I think that's what loneliness actually is it's not about being physically alone it's about the gap between the connection that you want and the connection that you have.
我觉得孤独就是这样：它不在于身体上是否独自一人，而在于你想要的联系与实际拥有的联系之间的差距。

26
00:02:26,359 --> 00:02:33,629
You can be surrounded by people and feel it you can be at a party and a conversation and still feel like you're watching your life through glass.
你身边有人也可能有这种感觉。在聚会或谈话中，你仍可能觉得自己隔着玻璃看着自己的人生。

27
00:02:33,639 --> 00:02:44,359
Alexa lights on okay it is 4 00 a m and we are up good morning everyone.
Alexa，开灯。好了，现在是凌晨四点，我们已经起来了。大家早上好。

28
00:02:44,359 --> 00:02:47,800
I am extremely jetlagged so we're working at 4 00 a m and getting our day started.
我时差特别严重，所以凌晨四点就在工作，开始新的一天。

29
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:50,359
I feel like when the sun isn't out I don't want to do anything.
我觉得太阳没出来时，我就什么都不想做。

30
00:02:50,359 --> 00:02:54,720
I don't understand how people get up so early because I feel like we should just be sleeping right now.
我不懂大家怎么能起那么早，因为我觉得我们现在应该还在睡觉。

31
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:04,640
Okay now we have the problem of breakfast I have not been home for a month so there's definitely no groceries in the fridge right now.
好了，现在遇到早餐问题了。我一个月没在家，所以冰箱里肯定没有食材。
